<DemoExample Title="Sticky" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" Id="example4" PreventRenderForMcpClient>
    <div>
        In Sticky mode, clicking an option selects it and renders it as the header button, removing it from the callout
        list while it stays selected. Split then makes the header a command of its own, running the
        selected item's action; without it the header only opens the menu.
    </div>
    <br />
    <div class="example-content">
        <BitMenuButton TItem="BitMenuButtonOption" Variant="BitVariant.Fill" Sticky>
            <BitMenuButtonOption Text="Option A" Key="A" />
            <BitMenuButtonOption Text="Option B" Key="B" IsEnabled="false" />
